{"schemaVersion":1,"storyId":"rhyme-sun-earth-and-moon","version":1,"title":"Sun, Earth and Moon (a poem)","ageTiers":["7-8","9-10"],"language":"en","narrationLocale":"en-GH","pages":[{"n":1,"text":"The Sun is a star that is far, far away,\nIt gives us the light and the warmth of day.","sentences":["The Sun is a star that is far, far away,\nIt gives us the light and the warmth of day."],"alt":"A bright sun over a village.","image":{"hash":"sha256:7e17647e6283456eb31ae193f82e2924b215aa619576a3dd52f379f951be6bc8","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:daabd91f8f5ecb17c10899503075fd3b7e036d0cf656a5ebf4cf00e42cc4486d","durationMs":11760,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,11760]],"words":[[0,508],[508,1015],[1015,1354],[1354,1523],[1523,2200],[2200,2877],[2877,3215],[3215,3976],[3976,4484],[4484,5415],[5415,5753],[5753,6599],[6599,6938],[6938,7445],[7445,8291],[8291,8799],[8799,9306],[9306,10322],[10322,10660],[10660,11760]]}}},{"n":2,"text":"The Earth is a ball that is turning round,\nOnce in a day, without a sound.","sentences":["The Earth is a ball that is turning round,\nOnce in a day, without a sound."],"alt":"A globe with a small arrow showing it turns.","image":{"hash":"sha256:2fd29cc8db328270defb0a5b0021a7c168057d780c815ff5e98afa9befd81c55","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:7d114655ee2b8fba7f0cdb0984f228daee79a413b51467bc87326623efaf3618","durationMs":13440,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,13440]],"words":[[0,645],[645,1720],[1720,2150],[2150,2365],[2365,3226],[3226,4086],[4086,4516],[4516,6021],[6021,7419],[7419,8279],[8279,8709],[8709,8924],[8924,9892],[9892,11397],[11397,11612],[11612,13440]]}}},{"n":3,"text":"When our side turns away, it is night,\nThe sky grows dark and the stars shine bright.","sentences":["When our side turns away, it is night,\nThe sky grows dark and the stars shine bright."],"alt":"A village at night with stars.","image":{"hash":"sha256:ccda4702ad6af8b8ac064da90f8f484166e76dd9b68d7973064ad9dd2501550e","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:2fbc2a2d0707a0c5bccf5a09662fa88cd22e5ff04847e7200a2a29635aa4efc1","durationMs":12240,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,12240]],"words":[[0,675],[675,1182],[1182,1857],[1857,2701],[2701,3630],[3630,3967],[3967,4305],[4305,5402],[5402,5909],[5909,6415],[6415,7260],[7260,7935],[7935,8441],[8441,8948],[8948,9792],[9792,10636],[10636,12240]]}}},{"n":4,"text":"The Moon goes round us, slow and wide,\nWith the Sun’s light shining on its side.","sentences":["The Moon goes round us, slow and wide,\nWith the Sun’s light shining on its side."],"alt":"The Moon above the Earth.","image":{"hash":"sha256:b3e0fd198beb73ef7d10d96e09843a6fcddcd40e244de3af52e8babefe2ee9ea","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:99938ec30cd3b47a8fc51f4bd7ff01119b980e5a99bb5afcf0aa039a330bd390","durationMs":11960,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,11960]],"words":[[0,532],[532,1240],[1240,1949],[1949,2835],[2835,3455],[3455,4164],[4164,4695],[4695,5670],[5670,6379],[6379,6910],[6910,7619],[7619,8505],[8505,9745],[9745,10100],[10100,10631],[10631,11960]]}}},{"n":5,"text":"So look and wonder, and ask and learn,\nThe sky has secrets for each in turn.","sentences":["So look and wonder, and ask and learn,\nThe sky has secrets for each in turn."],"alt":"A child looking up at the sky with a notebook.","image":{"hash":"sha256:1b668a1225b55ec7da24f06f6d870c2f08e533e5e1ec1a54366ff384121ba385","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:b1f41d3116dc4a504bf197392246b99d272a87f2950295d0e7adf637eb79238f","durationMs":12760,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,12760]],"words":[[0,396],[396,1187],[1187,1780],[1780,3264],[3264,3858],[3858,4451],[4451,5045],[5045,6331],[6331,6924],[6924,7518],[7518,8111],[8111,9496],[9496,10089],[10089,10881],[10881,11276],[11276,12760]]}}}],"activities":[{"id":"se-c1","type":"comprehension","afterPage":2,"question":"What makes day and night?","options":["The Earth turning","The Moon moving fast","The clouds"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"se-ph","type":"phonics","afterPage":1,"targetSound":"ay","prompt":"Which words rhyme with day?","options":["away","star","far"],"correctIndexes":[0]},{"id":"se-s1","type":"sequencing","prompt":"Put the poem’s ideas in order.","items":["The Sun gives light and warmth.","The Earth turns round.","Our side turns away and it is night.","The Moon goes round us."]},{"id":"se-sel","type":"sel","afterPage":5,"prompt":"How does it feel to wonder about the sky?","feelingOptions":["Curious","Amazed","Calm","Excited"]}],"glossary":[{"word":"star","definition":"A huge ball of hot, glowing gas far away in space; the Sun is one.","pages":[1]},{"word":"turning","definition":"Moving round and round.","pages":[2]},{"word":"Moon","definition":"The big round rock that goes around the Earth.","pages":[4]}],"assets":{"sha256:7e17647e6283456eb31ae193f82e2924b215aa619576a3dd52f379f951be6bc8":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/rhyme-sun-earth-and-moon/page1-1.webp","bytes":97716,"type":"image/webp"},"sha256:daabd91f8f5ecb17c10899503075fd3b7e036d0cf656a5ebf4cf00e42cc4486d":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/audio/daabd91f8f5e.mp3","bytes":94700,"type":"audio/mpeg"},"sha256:2fd29cc8db328270defb0a5b0021a7c168057d780c815ff5e98afa9befd81c55":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/rhyme-sun-earth-and-moon/page2-1.webp","bytes":118430,"type":"image/webp"},"sha256:7d114655ee2b8fba7f0cdb0984f228daee79a413b51467bc87326623efaf3618":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/audio/7d114655ee2b.mp3","bytes":108140,"type":"audio/mpeg"},"sha256:ccda4702ad6af8b8ac064da90f8f484166e76dd9b68d7973064ad9dd2501550e":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/rhyme-sun-earth-and-moon/page3-1.webp","bytes":79704,"type":"image/webp"},"sha256:2fbc2a2d0707a0c5bccf5a09662fa88cd22e5ff04